<!doctype html>
<!--
  The garden, walked.

  Three states on one page, because a walk is one thing and not three: the map
  of ten areas, one area with its plants in it, and one plant with a pad for
  stepping to its neighbours. Moving between them is a fragment change, so the
  back button behaves and a place can be linked to.

  Every area is a theme, and the ten are laid out from `Quotes.Theme.position`
  rather than arranged by hand — see docs/WEBSITE.md §"Walking it". Walking
  right goes from the still and long-span toward the moving and momentary,
  walking down from solitary toward shared.

  **Nothing here is published yet.** The plot service does not exist, so this
  draws from `plots.js`'s stand-in, and the page says so on the screen in as
  many words. The point of building it before the service is that the geometry,
  the pad and the keyboard walk can be argued about while they are still cheap
  to change.

  Static, like `/s`: no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party anything.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A garden of plants grown from meetings." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page" id="page">
      <header class="masthead">
        <img class="mark" src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
        <span class="wordmark" id="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
      </header>

      <!-- Said plainly, and not in small print. -->
      <p class="notice body" id="invented" hidden>
        Every plant here is invented. The garden is not open yet.
      </p>

      <!-- 1. The map: ten areas, five across and two down. -->
      <section class="garden-map" id="map" aria-label="The garden">
        <div class="garden-grid" id="map-grid"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. One area, and what stands in it. -->
      <section class="garden-area" id="area" hidden>
        <h1 class="heading" id="area-name"></h1>
        <div class="area-plot" id="area-plot" role="group"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. One plant, and the four ways out of it. -->
      <section class="garden-plant" id="plant" hidden>
        <p class="plant-name" id="plant-name"></p>
        <p class="label" id="plant-where"></p>

        <!--
          The line under the plant, drawn from the reader's own bank. Change the
          chooser and it says something else — not a translation, because no bank
          is a translation of another. docs/WEBSITE.md §"The garden, walked in
          one language at a time".
        -->
        <blockquote class="passage" id="passage" hidden>
          <p id="passage-text"></p>
          <footer class="label" id="passage-source"></footer>
        </blockquote>
        <div class="pad" id="pad" role="group">
          <button class="pad-key" type="button" data-go="up" aria-label="Up">↑</button>
          <button class="pad-key" type="button" data-go="left" aria-label="Left">←</button>
          <button class="pad-key" type="button" data-go="right" aria-label="Right">→</button>
          <button class="pad-key" type="button" data-go="down" aria-label="Down">↓</button>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!--
        The one control on this page that needs a word of its own. `g` is
        labelled by the wordmark above, which is a proper noun and travels; the
        four directions are labelled by the pad. This is the exception, and it
        earns a catalogue string rather than a hardcoded label in the script.
      -->
      <p class="garden-foot">
        <button class="quiet-button" type="button" id="random" data-s="random"></button>
      </p>

      <footer class="foot">
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg
              class="chooser__mark"
              viewBox="0 0 16 16"
              aria-hidden="true"
              focusable="false"
            >
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/walk.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
